// Shell-utils demo — daily-ten 13 Nov 2026 (library track).
// Verifies spawn.fg (roadmap item 55, shell-utils) over the
// run_command builtin: an echo whose output passes straight
// through to stdout, then exit codes for true/false and the
// bool helper. The echo is called FIRST on purpose: println
// output is stdio-buffered when piped, while the child
// process writes directly, so a later echo would overtake
// earlier printlns in the captured stream.
// Expected stdout:
// hello-shell
// 0
// 0
// 1
// true
import "spawn.fg";

fn main() {
    println(sh_echo("hello-shell"));
    println(sh_run("true"));
    println(sh_run("false"));
    println(sh_ok("true"));
}
